	abstract = {This paper is the first step in an attempt to reinterpret `trade' in early Greece. It is formulated as a theoretical sketch utilising only limited examples of supporting data: much more information could be assembled to back the arguments outlined here. I wish to try out a new way of looking at the phenomenon of expanding, cross-cultural, pan-Mediterranean contact and exchange which characterizes the late ninth through early fifth centuries BC, especially the later part of this time span for which evidence is more abundant. It would be wrong to imply that the character of contact and exchange was uniform}}

